+"""Session 5E-2d2 captures (brief section 7, "5E-2d1 LEFTOVERS"): one picture per reviewer note of Checkpoint 44, framed the same
+way before (a tree given with --root, e.g. `git archive origin/main`) and after, plus the colony on LOW.
+Shipped client (index.html), real renderer, scenario placements only (a jump, a camera framing, a UI tap). Software GL: looks
+and counts only, never a phone frame rate.
+usage: python3 dev/tests/conquest-leftovers-captures.py --mode world|town [--quality high|low] [--size 390x844] [--mouse]
+       [--out DIR] [--tag before|after] [--only name,name] [--root DIR] [--sharp] [--dpr 2]
+--mode world (the local economy; the pilot has no town): the see-through outline behind a thin thing and behind a building
+ (note 1), an atmosphere pylon's dome and the settler block (2), the map as it opens (3, 10), the objective beam (4), the Command
+ Base wall and towers (5: the art the style builds for a tier V base, stood on the base's own pad), steep banks (6), the colony
+ (LOW), the docked heat panel beside the POWER pill (10).
+--mode town (the real Worker on the fixture server, a fully built CC10 town): the town's miniature on the pad (8), the drive
+ view as it opens (9), the town's ground in the build view (7).
+Every run writes PNG pictures at the device's resolution and one JSON (draws, triangles, programs, the HUD boxes measured).
+Sizes used by the session: 390x844, 320x568 (touch) and 1366x768 (--mouse: keyboard + mouse)."""
